  "id": "thought-sampling",
  "term": "thought sampling",
  "definition": "Thought sampling is a method used during a task to capture a person’s subjective report of what they are thinking, such as whether their mind is wandering. In this context, it helps distinguish self-reported mental states from states inferred only from behavior.",
